& [AuthorityGrant] is exact
  + SOP is canonically a source-preserving multi-target semantic programming language
  + only explicit admitted program regions are executable candidates
  + one SemanticIR is the semantic center
  + exact semantics govern commitment and learned targets remain bounded proposals unless separately proved
  + target, runtime, compatibility, conformance, bootstrap, and proof obligations are canonical for future specification
  + [implementation_authority] is absent
  + [execution_authority] is absent
  + [runtime_authority] is absent
  + [provider_authority] is absent
  + [training_authority] is absent
  + [database_authority] is absent
  + [tool_authority] is absent
  + [hardware_authority] is absent
  + [deployment_authority] is absent
  + [effect_authority] is absent

& [Invalidation] is fail-closed
  + any locked artifact hash or byte drift
  + missing source, exploded, canonical, registry, matrix, or stage evidence
  + all-SOP execution default
  + role or region leakage
  + multiple incompatible SemanticIR meanings
  + hidden target loss, approximation, nondeterminism, or provider dependence
  + neural proposal promoted to fact, permission, or effect authority
  + bootstrap or independent-conformance erasure
  + implementation or external effect claimed under this signature
  + signature protocol change or superseding source

& [NextBoundary] is explicit
  + SMTC-SJS-01 may be consumed as language-purpose dependency by CTPR specification processing
  + no SMTC implementation worker is released by this phase lock
  + the minimum cross-target fixture requires separate source/profile authority and claimed implementation work
